{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514283-the-other-paths-of-humanity-in-the-modern-nights","id":1514283,"title":"The other paths of humanity in the modern nights","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-09T01:16:03-07:00","id":1514283,"title":"The other paths of humanity in the modern nights","content":"So, back in the dark ages the modern path of humanity was just one form of multiple paths. What do you think about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> 1) Whether the Paths of Breath, Community and Vigor might still exist in the Camarilla (and/or the Anarchs) - definitely not Illumination, though.<br /> <i>and;</i><br /> 2) Why the Camarilla appears to have chosen to pick the current interpretation of the road over other variants, which it appears to have outright discarded (Though, obviously, the meta reason is that VtM predates Dark Ages and that Humanity predates the <i>Via Humanitatis</i> and its derivative paths, so the Camarilla lacks the variants.)<br /> <br /> I'm kind of toying with giving Camarilla characters four paths to pick from (and an Anarch character I basically allow any path at all due to the presence of proselytizers and cults recruiting discreetly amongst them, including the Path of Illumination variant of humanity).<br /> <br /> I think, if you (re)define &quot;greater good&quot; and &quot;laws of the community&quot; as obeying the Traditions (the Masquerade, at least) or being loyal to the Anarch Movement, that the Path of Community might see more support that the Path of Humanity... Hell, define &quot;greater good&quot; as <i>&quot;kill the shit out of the Ancients&quot;</i> and &quot;laws&quot; as the Code of Milan it could <i>theoretically</i> make do in the Sabbat, if you don't plan to survive very long.<br /> <br /> Breath is... iffy. On the one hand, it requires you to get very good at hiding amongst the kine, which was the point of adopting humanity in the first place. On the other, being that involved with mortals makes you a much higher Masquerade breach, and shunning the advantage of your own powers puts you at such a disadvantage you're in trouble.<br /> <br /> Vigor might run into trouble for rocking the boat, but I still kind of like it. It's not a bad choice for the aging population though, once one starts getting weighed down by boredom and ennui.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T03:37:38-07:00","id":1514290,"title":"","content":"... I haven't heard of a lot of these paths. Is this first edition dark ages or something? <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I feel The Road of Kings and it's derivatives are the paths that most vampires should follow in modern nights. It's great for encouraging public order and it uses conscience so it isn't terribly far away from conventional human morality. I suspect some mortals heavily involved in violence like soldiers or gangsters would probably start their unlives on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T04:14:35-07:00","id":1514293,"title":"","content":"The followers of <b>Via Anima</b> (<b>Path of Breath</b>), the Inspired, try to find meaning and purpose among mortal men, sharing their burdens and daily lives. By doing so, they hope to cease being monsters in their own mind, and so stall off the Beast.<br /> - this could work in the Camarilla very well, even in the Anarch movement; as the book, DAV: Road of Humanity said, many who walk this path do so purely by instinct, never giving the matter much thought. Basically Humanity 0.1... or 2.0 depending of point of view<br /> <br /> The followers of<b> Via Communitas (Path of Community)</b>, the Civilised are more focused on the community as a whole, rather than individuals. They seldom strive to exalt themselves, and when they do it is usually as a means to benefit the community at large.<br /> - again, both in the Camarilla and Anarchs or even Sabat it could work<br /> <br /> <b>Via Vireo (Path of Vigor) </b>is a bit harder; the Rovers who follow the Path of Vigor are not only dedicated to an ideal of what humanity is, but also its nature. Rovers are drawn to the human tendency to innovate, expand its horizons, and move on for good or ill. The Path of Vigor is a forceful and energetic path that emphasizes motion and action before contemplation and stillness.<br /> - I don't think it would work in the Camarilla, the Ivory Tower is too... rigid, so to speak, and change is not the Cainite strong feature. The Anarchs, while well, anarchist and choitc, similarly can't handle well change and innovation, nature... but strangely, the Sabbat... I could see the Sabbat would adapt this in a twisted way, or even the original way, in the &quot;civilized&quot; parts of the Sabbat, the Prisci, the seasoned veterans, or even on the pack level, be civilized monsters, tempered by a Salubri Antitribu , Ventrue Antitribu or similar leader/priest with morals. The Sabbat in many ways are lot closer to humanity than the Camarilla or even the Anarchs, and Via Vireo could blossom and eventually lead to a more dangerous sabbat (if you want to distance yourself the me monster me kill you silly idea)<br /> <br /> The followers of the <b>Via Luminis</b> are a solitary lot, not necessarily by choice, but because society shuns them. Those who follow the Path of Illumination seek the Bitter Road to Golconda to leave the material world behind.<br /> - This... well technically could work in any sect to be honest. It is like having a Nodist in your city. An Illuminated could be usefull, even in the Sabbat, considering Ambrosio Luis Mon\u00e7ada and the others like him Faith and dedication, powerfull Cardinals and influental Sabbat members even could protect these seekers, like a Prince or Baron simply becasue they could serve as a deterrent example or a kind of test of Faith, the Devil's Advocate so to speak, someone who holds a broken mirror infront of the others and could be used as a kind of trial. As I said, like having a Nodist around. They could have their uses and thus survive or even thrive in a sect\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T04:19:43-07:00","id":1514295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514283-the-other-paths-of-humanity-in-the-modern-nights?p=1514290#post1514290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I haven't heard of a lot of these paths. Is this first edition dark ages or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they first appeared in Humanity's Road Book, and were also included in DAV20. Breath focuses on living as a human (as close as possible), amongst humans and rejecting vampirism as much as possible. Vigor rejects the concept of vampires as static and pushes for the embrace of change and new experiences. Community focuses on being part of a greater whole and putting the needs of your chosen community above yourself (as opposed to generic humanity, which favours the needs of everyone). Illumination declares god to be an evil, manipulative jackass who may not even be the real god, rejects him, denounces all authority (including other vampires) and focuses on pursuit wisdom, enlightenment and Golconda.<br /> <br /> Much as I enjoy the Road of Kings, I'm one of those killjoys who insists on Humanity only for Camarilla games. Sure, some Elders have enough power and clout to get away with it, but the pcs 99% of the time aren't one of them. That's why I'm thinking of compromise by adjusting Community; the path then holds you to Camarilla law and culture and the service/&quot;greater good&quot; of the local kindred community, gives you the bearing of humanity to help you blend in (which was the whole point of adapting to the Humanity en masse) and discourages being a selfish, murderous, Masquerade-breaching little criminal (paradoxical as that is for vampires)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T05:40:56-07:00","id":1514299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514283-the-other-paths-of-humanity-in-the-modern-nights?p=1514293#post1514293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the book, DAV: Road of Humanity said, many who walk this path do so purely by instinct, never giving the matter much thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually good to know. I've always wanted a way for thinbloods and most other &quot;unguided&quot; embraces to inevitably deteriorate into wassail without course correction. Making the Path of Breath the default &quot;morality&quot; for a fledgling who doesn't understand what they've become and keeps using their new cool superpowers, thus eroding their ability to resist going on frenzy-induced murder sprees, would work nicely.<br /> <br /> That said, I would not have any of these work in the Sabbat (which in my games is <i>heavily</i> dominated by the Path of Caine), except maybe as placeholders to stop you wassailing until you either die as canon fodder or get onto a &quot;real&quot; Path.<br /> The Noddists are primarily on the path whose rules include &quot;when you come across a vampire holding to humanity, <i>eat it</i>,&quot; and the non-Path of Caine in the Sabbat are busy drinking the Vampire Supremacy kool-aid and are likely to simply hand your diablerist a napkin or something.<br /> <br /> And in regards to the Blasphemers; they refuse to acknowledge any authority over themselves, with puts them at odds with the Camarilla too.\u200b Autarkis, Anarchs, or perhaps better yet, the Iconnu, are your better chances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-09-2023, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T05:47:03-07:00","id":1514300,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not familiar with these alternate Paths, but I really like what you guys have to say about them. I think I might include some of them in my game as heretical offshoots of Humanity which might be followed by some of the more mystically inclined among the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T20:44:40-07:00","id":1514545,"title":"","content":"Path of Vigor sounds really cool for younger Anarchs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}